{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01YHcmzVx4P7V1vYmz3F2SkJ", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marilyn_Diptych\"}, {\"url\": \"https://uen.pressbooks.pub/arth2720/chapter/andy-warhol-marilyn-monroe-diptych/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.wikipedia.com/wiki/Marilyn_Diptych\"}, {\"url\": \"https://news.artnet.com/art-world/before-netflix-warhol-tapped-into-the-tragic-mythos-of-marilyn-monroe-here-are-3-things-you-might-not-know-about-his-iconic-works-2188394\"}, {\"url\": \"https://news.artnet.com/art-world/before-netflix-warhol-tapped-into-the-tragic-mythos-of-marilyn-monroe-here-are-3-things-you-might-not-know-about-his-iconic-works-2188394?amp=1\"}, {\"url\": \"https://usaartnews.com/news/before-netflix-warhol-tapped-into-the-tragic-mythos-of-marilyn-monroehere-are-3-things-you-might-not-know-about-his-iconic-works\"}, {\"url\": \"https://WikiArt.org/en/andy-warhol/marilyn-diptych-1962\"}, {\"url\": \"https://usaartnews.com/news/before-netflix-warhol-tapped-into-the-tragic-mythos-of-marilyn-monroehere-are-3-things-you-might-not-know-about-his-iconic-works/amp\"}, {\"url\": \"https://lbas.lboro.ac.uk/poster/andy-warhol-marilyn-monroe-poster.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://artlovers.travel/en/artworks/marilyn-diptych\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:56:53.801Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Warhol Marilyn Diptych publicity photo film Niagara Monroe character", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01LWNcefDuCpUD9rYo4RW3fm", "content": [{"title": "Marilyn Diptych", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marilyn_Diptych"}, {"title": "Andy Warhol, Marilyn Monroe Diptych", "url": "https://uen.pressbooks.pub/arth2720/chapter/andy-warhol-marilyn-monroe-diptych/"}, {"title": "Marilyn Diptych", "url": "https://www.wikipedia.com/wiki/Marilyn_Diptych"}, {"title": "before netflix warhol tapped into the tragic mythos of marilyn monroe here are 3 things you might not know about his iconic works 2188394", "url": "https://news.artnet.com/art-world/before-netflix-warhol-tapped-into-the-tragic-mythos-of-marilyn-monroe-here-are-3-things-you-might-not-know-about-his-iconic-works-2188394"}, {"title": "before netflix warhol tapped into the tragic mythos of marilyn monroe here are 3 things you might not know about his iconic works 2188394", "url": "https://news.artnet.com/art-world/before-netflix-warhol-tapped-into-the-tragic-mythos-of-marilyn-monroe-here-are-3-things-you-might-not-know-about-his-iconic-works-2188394?amp=1"}, {"title": "before netflix warhol tapped into the tragic mythos of marilyn monroehere are 3 things you might not know about his iconic works", "url": "https://usaartnews.com/news/before-netflix-warhol-tapped-into-the-tragic-mythos-of-marilyn-monroehere-are-3-things-you-might-not-know-about-his-iconic-works"}, {"title": "marilyn diptych 1962", "url": "https://WikiArt.org/en/andy-warhol/marilyn-diptych-1962"}, {"title": "usaartnews.com", "url": "https://usaartnews.com/news/before-netflix-warhol-tapped-into-the-tragic-mythos-of-marilyn-monroehere-are-3-things-you-might-not-know-about-his-iconic-works/amp"}, {"title": "Andy Warhol Marilyn Monroe Poster", "url": "https://lbas.lboro.ac.uk/poster/andy-warhol-marilyn-monroe-poster.html"}, {"title": "Marilyn Diptych", "url": "https://artlovers.travel/en/artworks/marilyn-diptych"}]}, "The *Marilyn Diptych* (1962) is a silkscreen painting by Andy Warhol that uses a publicity still from the 1953 film *Niagara*. Created shortly after Monroe's death in August 1962, the work consists of fifty repeated images based on a publicity still from the 1953 film Niagara photographed by Gene Kornman. Its two panels are brightly colored portraits on the left and fading black-and-white impressions on the right.\n\nWarhol chose the photo himself. In August 1962, the same month that Monroe died of a sleeping pill overdose, Warhol sorted through his collection of photos of her and picked the publicity shot for Niagara taken by 20th Century Fox photographer Gene Korman (aka Eugene Kornman). He then cropped the photograph, closing in tightly around Monroe's signature look of blonde curls, dark eyebrows, sultry lips, and a beauty mark.\n\nOn the rights question, one source says the photo was owned and distributed by her movie studio. Another notes that Warhol's use of it resulted in a settlement with the owner of the Marilyn Monroe publicity photograph which he used as the source material for the paintings.\n\nThe sources spell the photographer's surname as both Kornman and Korman. Also, the Niagara publicity shots feature Monroe in a black halter dress with a white sailor collar, a costume she had also worn to the 1952 Miss America pageant (She wore this black dress with a plunging neckline and white sailor collar to the 1952 Miss America pageant, and again the following year when posing for Korman's publicity shots for Niagara.)."], "durationSeconds": 6.1693507909999985, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01YHcmzVx4P7V1vYmz3F2SkJ", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
